<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσ-φθέγγομαι</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτιφθ-</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			7.656
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Leon.
		</span></i>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>call to,
				address</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				331
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				1097
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Or.</u>
				481
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>salute</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῆμα</span>
			<u>AP</u> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>call by a name, call</i> so and so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ πάγον Κρόνου προσεφθέγξατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).50
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. μιᾷ κλήσει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					287e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>sound to, accompany</i>, [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλοὶ] π. χοροῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					4.81
				</span></i>
			.</div>
